{
  "opening": "The dateutil library is releasing version 0.13.2, which introduces several new features and fixes critical parsing behaviors. As the arrow project depends on dateutil, it must upgrade to this release to ensure compatibility with the updated public API and corrected edge cases in time zone and ISO 8601 parsing.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the relativedelta class must maintain its documented behavior for tuple-based initialization as described in its documentation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, when using parser.parse, if a tzinfos callable explicitly returns None, the function must not raise a ValueError but should handle the absence of timezone information gracefully."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the datetime_ambiguous, datetime_exists, and resolve_imaginary functions must correctly interpret datetime objects in relation to their associated tzinfo instances (tzfile, tzrange, or tzstr) without raising errors during inspection."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25",
      "text": "No observable behavioral changes are required for the consumer regarding the restructured documentation in the dateutil library."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser function must accept ISO 8601 time strings that use a comma as the decimal separator for fractional seconds."
    },
    {
      "id": "m37",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser function must treat T24:00 as representing midnight on the following day, compliant with ISO 8601 standards."
    },
    {
      "id": "m41",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, tzoffset and tzfile must support sub-minute time zone offsets (e.g., 30 minutes) in Python 3.6 and newer versions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m43",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser.parse_isotime method must correctly handle time strings where the hour component is 24, interpreting them as midnight of the next day."
    },
    {
      "id": "m53",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparse function must accept more than six fractional digits in the seconds portion of an ISO 8601 time string."
    },
    {
      "id": "m58",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, tzfile must correctly handle base offset changes during Daylight Saving Time transitions, specifically fixing issues related to Samoan time zone offset changes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m66",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, both isoparser and parser must accept 'z' (lowercase Z) as a valid indicator for UTC time zones in ISO 8601 strings."
    },
    {
      "id": "m68",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, the cache_clear and set_cache_size functions must be available to manage the LRU cache for tzoffset, tzstr, and gettz, ensuring transient references do not prevent garbage collection."
    },
    {
      "id": "m80",
      "text": "In the dateutil library, rrule and rruleset must support parsing EXDATE parameters from RRULE strings, allowing exclusion dates to be correctly identified during rule generation."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure the arrow project's dependencies are updated to reflect these changes in dateutil 0.13.2. This will guarantee that all time parsing and recurrence rule functionalities operate according to the latest specifications."
}
